summary:
  The box a drawing is rendered into is square whatever its shape.

history:
  Cropped to a square box, a drawing of 200 by 80 is rendered 1500 by
  600: its shape is kept, and the source size is not. A drawing of 109 to
  1 is then read at 65400 by 600, 157 MB, just under the side Qt refuses
  (measured in Qt 6.12). The box has the drawing's own shape, so cropping
  to it cuts nothing and nothing is read larger than the source size. This
  mutant makes the box square.

target:
  package/contents/ui/CoverLogic.js

find:
      return { "width": Math.round(w * k), "height": Math.round(h * k) };

replace:
      return { "width": Math.round(Math.max(w, h) * k), "height": Math.round(Math.max(w, h) * k) };

expect:
  Killed by tests/test_cover_larger_fetch.py::test_a_drawing_from_the_network_is_asked_for_its_shape_once,
  which runs first, with a drawing from the network, and behind it by
  tests/qml/tst_coverlogic.qml::test_a_drawing_gets_a_box_of_its_own_shape_inside_the_source_size,
  which asks for the box itself.
  Line-neutral.
